# What the `.dbd` does not carry: the type AND the `special` of a
# `special(SPC_DBADDR)` field. Same grammar and same purpose as
# `crates/epics-base-rs/dbd/cvt_dbaddr.types` — read that file's header for the
# reasoning; this one covers only the record types declared in THIS crate's
# `dbd/` directory.
#
# record.FIELD          DBF type        special     dyn         C source

# mca: the spectrum (VAL) and the ROI background curve (BG) are both allocated
# `NMAX` deep with the element width of `FTVL`, and `cvt_dbaddr` re-points the
# field at `bptr` / `pbg` and re-types it from FTVL on every name resolution:
#
#     paddr->no_elements   = pmca->nmax;
#     paddr->field_type    = pmca->ftvl;
#     paddr->dbr_field_type = pmca->ftvl;
#
# so the DBF_NOACCESS in the `.dbd` is the placeholder for the `void *` C member,
# not the served type. `dyn = FTVL` marks both as runtime-typed: the declared
# type below is only FTVL's own `initial("5")` default (DBF_LONG), and the
# record's stored element type wins at serve time.
mca.VAL                 DBF_LONG        SPC_DBADDR  FTVL        mcaRecord.c:847-863
mca.BG                  DBF_LONG        SPC_DBADDR  FTVL        mcaRecord.c:847-863
